From 1ad73c13508fd832a983af8d53ac53ac6368fd4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:36:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a worker parking its own card on an opaque probe
 must name the producer (opaque_probe_wait); same-probe re-parks count as one
 premise [daveey]

A wake check that names no card or CI run proves only that something polls. On 10-27 macbook
t_3b031dd1 parked 9 h (and ~24 h on 10-26) on a python3 probe for 'agent Chrome and ports
9333/9334 gone' while a launchd KeepAlive job kept that browser up; kanban_wait_info already
called such parks agent-owned stalls, but the park gate (_infer) recorded them as inferred
external waits and accepted them.

- _infer refuses a card's own worker parking on an opaque probe with no declared awaiting
  (code opaque_probe_wait; uses kanban_wait_info.producer_from_wake_check so writer and
  checker agree). The error says how to declare awaiting={kind:'external', ref, why}, to do
  the action or create an owner card, or to use a needs_input block. Short continues
  (<= 2 h) and operator parks (dashboard, terminal: no HERMES_KANBAN_TASK for that card) are
  unchanged; operator parks still record an inferred wait the checker flags.
- Repeat counting also keys on the whitespace-normalised opaque probe, so a third park on
  the same probe escalates to an owner card however the reason is worded.
- kanban_tools_schemas: wake_check says a probe alone is not a producer.
- Tests: refusal on schedule/block/long continue + a real hub probe shape; declared external
  parks; CI/wait-check/short-continue/clock controls; re-worded re-park escalates; worker CLI
  refused vs operator park accepted. Wake-check mechanism tests declare their producer.

Self-heal kanban-92e96c16fd (t_01a180b0c3a4ca5e).
